-- title:
--   Finite homogeneous quotient puts powers of each coordinate in the ideal
-- statement:
--   For a polynomial ideal generated by polynomials homogeneous of a common strictly positive weighted degree, finite dimension of the quotient implies that a positive power of every coordinate variable belongs to the ideal.
-- source:
--   openai/math Ampleness stack: WeightedIdealCurveBound implies eps-ample exceptional twist, hence Serre vanishing and eventual generation of I^n by weight ≤ n(rho+eps) sections.

